****************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
All git Commands:
****************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
1.git fetch : Download the latest changes from the Remote Repository
2.git diff : Show File Differences not yet Staged
3.git checkout -b <branch_name> : create and switch to new branch
4.git checkout <branch_name> : Switch to an existing branch
5.git squash : combining multiple commits into single one
6.git commit --amend : Modify the last commit
7.git reset -hard : resets everything to a previous commit, erasing all uncommitted changes
8.git push origin <branch_name> : push a branch to a remote 
9.git status : show the state of your working directory
10.git commit -a -m "commit message" :commit all tracked changes with a message
11.git add <file_path> : add files to a staging area 
12.git pull : fetch and merge remote changes
13.git stash : stash changes for later
14.git format -patch -1 <commit_id> : create a patch file for a specific commit 
15.git show <commit_id> : show details about a commit 
16.git reset HEAD~1 :undo the last commit, preserving the changes locally 
17.git apply <patch_file_name> : apply changes from a patch file 
18.git branch -d <branch_name> : delete a branch forcefully 
19.git reset : undo commits by moving branch reference 
20.git clone : create a local copy of a remote repo.
21.git rebase -i : Rebase interactively, rewrite commit history
22.git cherry-pick <commit_id> : Apply changes from a specific commit 
23.git revert : undo commits by creating a new commit 
24.git merge : merge branches together 
25.git log -stat : show commit logs with stats
26.git stash pop : apply and remove stashed changes
27.git branch : lists branches
28.git restore . : revert all the changes
29.git clean –f : revert or remove all the changes
29.git push origin --delete <branch_name> : delete the pushed branch on the git 
